---
title: Red Wine Poached Pear with Candied Almonds and Mascarpone
Rating: 10/10
description: Holy crap, is this ever good! May need to limit almond extract in filling if you have a potent or good quality extract, or just like it less.
source.name: USA Pears
source.url: https://usapears.org/recipe/red-wine-poached-pear-with-mascarpone-and-candied-almonds/
tags: Alcohol, Desserts
---

= Pears =
Peel and core @pears{6}(Bosc, Anjou, or Bartlett). 
To retain pear shape, insert and twist a corer or pairing knife from several
angles at the bottom of the pear to extract core and seeds.

In a #saucepan{} just big enough to hold the pears, combine
@red wine{750%ml}(Zinfandel or other spiced varietal), @sugar{2%cup},
@Chinese Five Spice{2%Tbsp}, @cinnamon{1%tsp}, and @ground cloves{1%tsp}.
Add pears and just enough @water or additional wine to cover pears.

Bring to a boil. 
Cover and simmer over low heat until pears are tender but not falling apart,
about ~{30%minutes} depending on ripeness of pears.

> Alternate method: Place pears in a deep baking dish. Pour wine mixture over pears,
> cover and bake at 350°F, turning pears periodically until evenly cooked through, about 1 hour.

Remove pears from wine mixture. 
Cool to room temperature then cover and refrigerate until completely chilled.

Simmer wine mixture until reduced to a syrupy consistency (~{1%hour} or more).
Set aside until ready to use.

= Candied Almonds =
Preheat oven to 350°F. 
In a bowl mix @almonds{1%cup}(sliced, untoasted), @sugar{2%tbsp} and @water{2%tbsp}.

Spread on a parchment or foil-lined baking sheet. 
Bake ~{15-20%minutes}, turning several times until almonds are golden brown and sugar is caramelized. 
Cool.

= Filling =
Place @Mascarpone Cheese{8%oz}, @heavy cream{1/4%cup}, @powdered sugar{1/4%cup},
and @almond extract{1%tsp} in a #large mixing bowl{}.
Whip on high speed until mixture forms firm peaks. 
Can be made up to 12 hours ahead, covered and refrigerated.

= To serve =
Place mascarpone filling in a pastry bag with decorative tip. 
Pipe or spoon 2 tablespoons filling into center of each pear. 
Place on dessert plates. 

Pipe 2 tablespoons filling around bottom of pears, or garnish with a dollop. 
Drizzle slightly warmed wine syrup over each pear.
Garnish with candied almonds and serve immediately.
